{
  "title": "VOYAGER: An Open-Ended Embodied Agent with Large Language Models",
  "authors": [
    "Guanzhi Wang",
    "Yuqi Xie",
    "Yunfan Jiang",
    "Ajay Mandlekar",
    "Chaowei Xiao",
    "Yuke Zhu",
    "Linxi \"Jim\" Fan",
    "Anima Anandkumar"
  ],
  "year": 2023,
  "arxivId": "2305.16291",
  "abstract": "VOYAGER is an embodied agent that uses large language models to continuously explore the world, acquire diverse skills, and make new discoveries without human intervention. It consists of three key components: an automatic curriculum that maximizes exploration, a skill library for storing and retrieving complex behaviors, and an iterative prompting mechanism that incorporates environment feedback, execution errors, and self-verification for program improvement.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "VOYAGER is an embodied agent that uses large language models to explore the world and acquire new skills. It's designed to be a **lifelong learner**, meaning it can continuously learn and improve without human intervention. The key idea is to use a combination of **automatic curriculum**, **skill library**, and **iterative prompting mechanism** to enable the agent to learn and adapt in an open-ended environment.",
