    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "The automatic curriculum proposes new tasks for the agent to complete, which are then used to generate executable code through the iterative prompting mechanism. The skill library stores and retrieves complex behaviors, allowing the agent to build upon previously learned skills. The iterative prompting mechanism incorporates environment feedback, execution errors, and self-verification to refine the generated code.",
